ind the site content.","elements":[{"form":"silhouette","name":"Mountain and sun landscape","role":"illustration","depth":0,"anchor":"behind","motion":"Slow parallax: the ridges drift a few pixels with scroll and pointer, and the sun's glow breathes gently.","render":"The user's three strokes become one continuous vista: the left ridge (R1) and right ridge (R2) filled as layered mountain silhouettes in deep teal and slate, with the sun arc (R3) as a warm amber disc glowing between the peaks; the whole scene sits on a dark night-sky background ","regions":[1,2,3],"section":"Hero","placement":"section-background"}]},"generic":"A travel booking site with a dark navy background, a single warm orange accent, a generic sans-serif hero, and a row of identical rounded cards with soft shadows for destinations.","palette":{"text":"#F2EBDD","accent":"#E8A33D","surface":"#16283C","secondary":"#7FB069","background":"#0E1B2C"},"styleId":"elegant_serif","summary":"A fluid, elegant travel-booking site for high-altitude and wilderness tours, where a hand-drawn mountain-and-sun landscape sits as the living background behind all scrolling content.","audience":"Independent travellers and small groups (25–55) who book guided expeditions, multi-day treks and scenic tours, and want to feel the scale of a place before they","sections":[{"name":"Navigation","purpose":"Slim top bar with the Meridian Trails wordmark, links to Expeditions, Journal, About and a Book a tour button."},{"name":"Hero","purpose":"Full-bleed first screen over the drawn landscape: a large editorial headline naming the brand's promise, a one-line subhead, and the primary Book a tour action."},{"name":"Expeditions","purpose":"Three featured tours — the Karakoram Traverse, the Dolomites High Route and the Atacama Sky Camp — each with distance, days, altitude and a starting price."},{"name":"Journal","purpose":"Editorial field notes: three recent dispatches from the trail with dates and short standfirsts."},{"name":"About","purpose":"Who guides the routes: the founding guides, years in the field, and the small-team promise."},{"name":"Booking","purpose":"A booking form: choose expedition, dates, party size and a contact field, with a confirm button."},{"name":"Footer","purpose":"Brand mark, contact details, social links and a fine-print line."}],"signature":"The user's three drawn strokes — two ridges and a sun arc — rendered as a fluid, parallaxing SVG landscape that stays fixed behind all content and subtly shifts with scroll and pointer.","primaryAction":"Book a tour"}}